---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="AHGadget | Projects | Wretzelectronics">
  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="detail-header">
      <h1 class="project-title">AHGadget</h1>
      <p class="project-tagline">Multi-protocol wireless exploration and power-monitoring platform.</p>
      <div class="tag-row">
        <span class="tag-badge">Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">ESP32-S3</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">Python / Kivy</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">CC1101 RF</span>
        <span class="tag-badge">INA219</span>
      </div>

      <div class="action-row">
        <a 
          href="https://github.com/wretzel01/AHGadget" 
          target="_blank" 
          rel="noopener noreferrer" 
          class="cyber-button"
        >
          <svg class="github-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18">
            <path fill="currentColor" d="M12 0C5.37 0 0 5.37 0 12c0 5.31 3.435 9.795 8.205 11.385.6.105.825-.255.825-.57 0-.285-.015-1.23-.015-2.235-3.015.555-3.795-.735-4.035-1.41-.135-.345-.72-1.41-1.23-1.695-.42-.225-1.02-.78-.015-.795.945-.015 1.62.87 1.845 1.23 1.08 1.815 2.805 1.305 3.495.99.105-.78.42-1.305.765-1.605-2.67-.3-5.46-1.335-5.46-5.925 0-1.305.465-2.385 1.23-3.225-.12-.3-.54-1.53.12-3.18 0 0 1.005-.315 3.3 1.23.96-.27 1.98-.405 3-.405s2.04.135 3 .405c2.295-1.56 3.3-1.23 3.3-1.23.66 1.65.24 2.88.12 3.18.765.84 1.23 1.905 1.23 3.225 0 4.605-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.925.435.375.81 1.095.81 2.22 0 1.605-.015 2.895-.015 3.3 0 .315.225.69.825.57A12.02 12.02 0 0024 12c0-6.63-5.37-12-12-12z"/>
          </svg>
          <span>View Source on GitHub</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="hero-image-wrapper">
      <img src="/images/projects/ahgadget.png" alt="AHGadget main photo" class="detail-hero-img" />
    </div>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Overview</h2>
      <p>
        AHGadget is a handheld multi‑protocol wireless exploration device that brings IR, RF, BLE, Wi‑Fi, and power‑monitoring tools into a single platform. 
        The prototype implements all major subsystems and workflows, but it has not yet been built into a final enclosure or PCB.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        The system uses a dual‑processor design. A Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W handles the UI, scanning, and high‑level logic. 
        An ESP32‑S3 manages timing‑critical IR and RF operations, BLE advertisement parsing, and power telemetry. 
        Both processors communicate through a structured IPC channel.
      </p>

      <div class="diagram-block">
        <h3>Communication Architecture</h3>
        <p class="diagram-caption">
          Interaction between the Pi Zero 2 W, ESP32‑S3, CC1101, INA219, IR subsystem, and Wi‑Fi adapter through the IPC channel.
        </p>
        <img src="/images/projects/ahgadget-architecture.png" alt="AHGadget architecture diagram" class="diagram-img" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Hardware Design</h2>
      <p>
        AHGadget integrates multiple wireless modules into a single working prototype. 
        The hardware stack includes the touchscreen, Pi Zero 2 W, ESP32‑S3, CC1101 RF module, INA219 power monitor, IR subsystem, and external Wi‑Fi adapter. 
        A proper PCB and enclosure are planned for a future version.
      </p>

      <div class="diagram-grid">
        <div class="diagram-block">
          <h3>Enclosure Design</h3>
          <p class="diagram-caption">Initial layout for the touchscreen, Pi, ESP32‑S3, RF module, and power system.</p>
          <img src="/images/projects/ahgadget-enclosure.png" alt="AHGadget enclosure design" class="diagram-img" />
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-block">
          <h3>Hardware Stack</h3>
          <p class="diagram-caption">Assembled prototype showing module placement and interconnects.</p>
          <img src="/images/projects/ahgadget-stack.png" alt="AHGadget hardware stack" class="diagram-img" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="diagram-block full-width">
        <h3>Wiring Diagram</h3>
        <p class="diagram-caption">Electrical wiring and power routing across all subsystems.</p>
        <img src="/images/projects/ahgadget-wiring.png" alt="AHGadget wiring diagram" class="diagram-img" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section cyber-card">
      <h2>Software Architecture</h2>
      <p>
        The software includes a Python/Kivy UI on the Pi, custom ESP‑IDF firmware on the ESP32‑S3, and an IPC channel for JSON commands, subsystem events, and binary RF frames.
      </p>

      <div class="diagram-grid">
        <div class="diagram-block">
          <h3>Data Flow Diagram</h3>
          <p class="diagram-caption">Data pathways between the UI, IPC channel, and sensor hardware.</p>
          <img src="/images/projects/ahgadget-dataflow.png" alt="AHGadget data flow diagram" class="diagram-img" />
        </div>

        <div class="diagram-block">
          <h3>System State Machine</h3>
          <p class="diagram-caption">Transitions between idle, scan, capture, replay, and power‑monitor states.</p>
          <img src="/images/projects/ahgadget-statemachine.png" alt="AHGadget system state machine" class="diagram-img" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .project-detail {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .detail-header {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .project-title {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .project-tagline {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tag-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

/* Header Action Bar & GitHub Button */
  .action-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    width: 100%;
  }

  a.cyber-button,
  a.cyber-button:link,
  a.cyber-button:visited {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #ffffff !important;
    background: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-neon, #00f0ff);
    border-radius: 6px;
    text-decoration: none !important;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);
  }

  a.cyber-button:hover {
    background: rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.2);
    box-shadow: 0 0 18px var(--border-glow, rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.6));
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    color: var(--border-neon, #00f0ff) !important;
  }

  .github-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    fill: currentColor;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .hero-image-wrapper {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.2);
    background: #000;
  }

  .detail-hero-img {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 480px;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 240, 255, 0.15);
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .content-section p {
    color: var(--text-main, #e2e8f0);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .diagram-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .diagram-block {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .diagram-block h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--border-neon, #00f0ff);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .diagram-caption {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem !important;
  }

  .diagram-img {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    background: #000;
    display: block;
  }
</style>